---
metadata: {
    partial_name: "Rate Limit | Allow",
}
---
{%- comment -%}
  Counts recent attempts at an action and records this one if it is allowed. Called with:
    function allowed = 'account/rate_limit/allow', action: 'sign_in', key: email, max_per_key: 10, max_per_ip: 50
  @params
    action      - sign_in, otp, forgot_password, email_check, sign_in_link, sign_in_code, sign_in_code_check
    key         - what the attempt is about (email or user id); blank limits by IP only
    max_per_key - attempts allowed per key in the window
    max_per_ip  - attempts allowed per IP address in the window
    window      - seconds, default 900 (15 minutes)
    count_only  - true to check without recording this attempt (the caller records failures itself)
  Returns true when the attempt may go ahead, false when a limit is reached.
  A refused attempt is not recorded, so a blocked caller cannot extend its own lockout.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign window = window | default: 900
  assign count_only = count_only | default: false
  assign key = key | default: '' | append: '' | downcase | strip
  function ip = 'account/rate_limit/client_ip'

  assign now_unix = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
  assign since_iso = now_unix | minus: window | date: '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'

  graphql counts = 'account/rate_limit/count_attempts', action: action, key: key, ip: ip, since: since_iso

  if counts.for_ip.total_entries >= max_per_ip
    return false
  endif
  if key != blank and counts.for_key.total_entries >= max_per_key
    return false
  endif

  comment
    count_only: true checks the limit without recording, for callers that record only
    failures (sign-in records a wrong password, not a correct one).
  endcomment
  if count_only != true
    function recorded = 'account/rate_limit/record', action: action, key: key, window: window
  endif
  return true
-%}
